  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_006 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653. Image-only with resnet50 was very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality's contribution is uncertain. The critical open question is whether multimodal fusion can improve upon the strong RNA-only baseline, and whether a stronger image encoder (ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet) changes that picture. This experiment (config_038) takes the exact best RNA setup (scvi_n200, multiprofile, transformer) and adds imagenet_vit_l with concat fusion, directly testing whether the image modality provides complementary signal when paired with the strongest RNA representation. It is the best use of this slot because: (1) it isolates the effect of adding image to our proven best RNA config, (2) ViT-L is the strongest available image encoder so it gives the image modality its best chance, (3) concat is the simplest fusion, reducing confounds, and (4) the answer determines whether the remaining 3 experiments should explore further multimodal variants or stay in the RNA-only space."
}

